# The full pre-commit check set, plus the test suite, the browser suite, and a
# production build.
#
# Deliberately not a lighter version of pre-commit (spec Edge Cases): the same
# lint/type steps run again, because what was committed one file at a time
# still has to hold together as a whole before it leaves the machine.
#
# The unit test suite lives here and only here. It is one of the two slowest
# checks of the set, and paying it per commit taxed the small, frequent
# commits a commit-time gate should stay clear of; running it once per push
# keeps the guarantee that matters — nothing reaches the remote with a
# failing test.
#
# lint runs unscoped here — there are no "staged files" during a push, so the
# whole project is linted rather than a diff.
#
# The design-system audit joins here, and only here, as of feature 010. It was
# left out of the hooks entirely when it was written, for a good reason: it
# failed on every run, so as a gate it would have been noise a developer learns
# to skip. The tree passes it now, which is what makes it a gate rather than a
# complaint. Tree-wide, so pre-push rather than pre-commit, and 0.05s beside a
# next build.
#
# E2E joins here as of the constitution's 2.3.0 amendment (Principle V),
# reversing the position held through v2.2.2 and 009's FR-007. The reasoning
# for keeping it manual-only never stopped being true — there is still no CI,
# so this cost still lands entirely on whoever is pushing — but the suite has
# since caught a real accessibility regression and one of its own tests that
# could not fail (specs/012-browser-e2e-tests, PR #26 review round), and that
# record moved the trade. Still not in pre-commit: a browser suite is the
# wrong cost to pay on every small commit, the same reasoning that already
# kept `npm test` out of it.
#
# A dedicated port and a forced fresh build, not the defaults `npm run
# test:e2e` uses standalone: this hook must test the code actually being
# pushed, not whatever a stray `next dev` elsewhere on the machine happens to
# be serving on 3000 — the exact bug the config's `E2E_FRESH_BUILD`/`PORT`
# escape hatches exist for (research.md §8). The full statement of where this
# suite runs, and the condition for reconsidering this again, is
# specs/012-browser-e2e-tests/contracts/run-location.md.

echo "▶ lint         (eslint, whole project, warnings fail)"
npx eslint --max-warnings=0 || { echo "✖ pre-push failed at: lint"; exit 1; }

echo "▶ typecheck    (tsc --noEmit, whole project)"
npm run typecheck || { echo "✖ pre-push failed at: typecheck"; exit 1; }

echo "▶ test         (vitest run, whole project)"
npm test || { echo "✖ pre-push failed at: test"; exit 1; }

echo "▶ design-system (audit, whole tree)"
npm run audit:design-system || { echo "✖ pre-push failed at: design-system"; exit 1; }

echo "▶ build        (next build, production)"
npm run build || { echo "✖ pre-push failed at: build"; exit 1; }

echo "▶ e2e          (playwright, fresh build, dedicated port)"
PORT=3100 E2E_FRESH_BUILD=1 npm run test:e2e || { echo "✖ pre-push failed at: e2e"; exit 1; }

echo "✔ pre-push passed"
